#: ../../source/reference/design/pages.md:1
msgid "The page is the unit of work"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/pages.md:3
msgid ""
"*Implemented.* This is the assumption everything else in the engine rests"
" on, and the one worth understanding before any other."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/pages.md:6
msgid "The assumption: a page carries its own context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/pages.md:7
msgid "**A page carries the context needed to understand what is on it.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/pages.md:9
msgid ""
"A document is opened once, through PyMuPDF, and immediately becomes a "
"sequence of native pages. From that point nothing downstream knows a PDF "
"reader was involved. Each page is then processed **on its own**, with no "
"knowledge of the pages before or after it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/pages.md:13
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The assumption is restrictive, and it is deliberately restrictive. It is "
"false of some pages of some reports, and the engine does not pretend "
"otherwise — see {doc}`promises` for what happens there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/pages.md:16
msgid "What the page assumption makes possible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/pages.md:17
msgid ""
"Three good properties, and they are not independent benefits so much as "
"three faces of the same one:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/pages.md:19
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Work divides.** Nothing in the description of the algorithm mentions "
"threads or processes, and that is why parallelism could be added without "
"redesigning anything: pages that do not depend on each other can be "
"processed in any order, anywhere. See {doc}`parallelism`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/pages.md:23
msgid ""
"**A page is a testable unit.** A format's behaviour on one page can be "
"frozen as a fixture and checked in isolation — this is exactly what "
"`freeports-dev make-tests` writes, three JSON files per page, one per "
"segment. A regression tells you *which segment* of *which page* changed, "
"rather than that a 1,800-page document now produces a different table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/pages.md:28
msgid ""
"**A failure is local.** A page the engine cannot read is a page that is "
"skipped, with a log row naming it and a coordinate inside it. It is not a"
" run that dies, and it is not a silent hole either."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/pages.md:31
msgid "What the page assumption costs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/pages.md:32
msgid "The cost is real and is paid in two places."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/pages.md:34
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Some values genuinely are not on the page.** A fund name printed once "
"on the section's cover, a currency declared in a heading forty pages "
"earlier. The assumption says nothing about these, and the answer is not "
"to weaken it — see {doc}`promises`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/pages.md:38
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Some layouts encode meaning in sequence.** \"This table continues from "
"the previous page\" is a fact about a pair of pages, not about a page. "
"The engine's answer is to confine that reasoning to **classification**, "
"where a per-document finalizer may look at the whole sequence, and to "
"keep it out of extraction entirely. See {doc}`classification`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/pages.md:43
msgid "The rejected alternative: a second pass over the document"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/pages.md:44
msgid ""
"A second pass over the document: read it once to gather context, once "
"more to use it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/pages.md:46
#, python-format
msgid ""
"It was rejected because it doubles the most expensive part of a run — PDF"
" loading and page parsing are 35–75% of a job — to serve a minority of "
"values, and because it reintroduces exactly the ordering dependency "
"between pages that this assumption exists to remove. Once page 412 needs "
"page 3 to have been read first, work no longer divides, a page is no "
"longer a testable unit, and a failure is no longer local. All three "
"properties go at once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/pages.md:52
msgid "Promises keep them. That is the whole argument for them."
msgstr ""

